api.github.com/users/myang2021/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myang2021/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-05T19:18:08Z","updated_at":"2024-04-08T18:32:11Z","closed_at":"2024-04-08T18:32:11Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-10751](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-10751)\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIn recent debugging of a catalog version related bug, I noticed the following logs:\r\n\r\n```\r\nI0401 18:37:02.763697 353140 tablet_server.cc:897] set pg_yb_catalog_version table in global mode\r\nI0401 18:37:02.763732 353140 tablet_server.cc:887] set pg_yb_catalog_version table in perdb mode\r\n```\r\n\r\nThese two logs appear back-to-back. However the test uses per-database catalog version mode from the beginning and there is no such moment that we change from global mode to per-db mode. This is a code bug that while we go through the list of db catalog versions retrieved from the tserver-master heartbeat response, we prematurely set to global mode after processing the very first database item.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Issue Type\r\n\r\nkind/bug\r\n\r\n### Warning: Please confirm that this issue does not contain any sensitive information\r\n\r\n- [X] I confirm this issue does not contain any sensitive information.\r\n\r\n[DB-10751]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-10751?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","closed_by":{"login":"myang2021","id":79478033,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NDc4MDMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79478033?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myang2021","html_url":"https://github.com/myan